# Shared AI Rules (mandatory)

For work in `dent1`, use the shared rule indexes in `ai-rules` as the starting point before making substantial changes.

- For Angular or frontend work, read `C:\Users\rishi.alluri\OneDrive - McKissock LP\Documents\Projects\ai-rules\frontend\00-index\frontend-rules-index.md` first.
- For API or backend work, read `C:\Users\rishi.alluri\OneDrive - McKissock LP\Documents\Projects\ai-rules\backend\index.md` first.
- If a task touches both frontend and backend, consult both indexes before implementing.
- Use each index to choose only the specific rule files relevant to the current task instead of reading every rule file.
- Treat the linked shared rules as the default guidance for architecture, placement, naming, auth, DTOs, API contracts, testing, and similar area-specific decisions.
- When frontend rules use placeholder names, replace them with the actual `dent1` naming and business-area names used in this repository.
